A directed network of underground water pipes with varying capabilities (L/min) is shown in the diagram below.

\exfigure{717_q39_1}

Insert the minimum cut on the network diagram above and hence, calculate the maximum flow of water through the network of pipes from the source to the sink.

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{717_q39_s1}

The maximum flow equals the capacity of the minimum cut.
$$\text{Maximum flow} = 6+6+2 = 14 \text{ L/min}$$
